message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Horizon-Uniform Prediction on Operator-Generated Networks (simulation and supplementary materials)"
authors:
  - family-names: Nechesov
    given-names: Andrey
    affiliation: "Artificial Intelligence Center, Novosibirsk State University"
  - family-names: Puzarenko
    given-names: Vadim
    affiliation: "Sobolev Institute of Mathematics, SB RAS; Artificial Intelligence Center, Novosibirsk State University"
year: 2026
license: MIT
keywords:
  - polynomial-time computability
  - direct limits
  - predictive analytics
  - evolving networks
  - fixed-point theorems
abstract: >
  Deterministic simulation validating the complexity guarantees of the paper
  "Polynomial-Time Predictive Analytics on Evolving Networks via p-Computable
  Direct Limits" (IEEE Access submission, 2026): linear-in-horizon
  materialization, look-ahead-linear query cost, horizon-uniform query time
  under network growth, a boundary-condition ablation, and a confidence-floor
  validity check.
